WEBVTT

00:00.412 --> 00:01.192
[SPEAKER_00]: Third of Wealsun.

00:03.153 --> 00:13.678
[SPEAKER_00]: As the sun sets in the west, Gouge pulls him out of the bar to an alleyway and sits him down to have a little talk.

00:19.361 --> 00:20.382
[SPEAKER_02]: Know what you're trying to do?

00:20.402 --> 00:21.342
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you like the song?

00:22.803 --> 00:27.325
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, fucking loved it actually, but saw it didn't go over while reading the room.

00:29.023 --> 00:33.067
[SPEAKER_02]: And took it upon myself to get your ass out of there the best way I could.

00:33.807 --> 00:35.789
[SPEAKER_02]: Everyone was kind of stunned looking at you.

00:37.311 --> 00:39.432
[SPEAKER_02]: So I made a bigger scene.

00:40.934 --> 00:43.016
[SPEAKER_02]: Showing a little blade and grabbing you and taking you out.

00:44.457 --> 00:48.941
[SPEAKER_02]: Obviously looked at Ty because they know he was with you.

00:49.241 --> 00:50.482
[SPEAKER_02]: Told them to sit the fuck down.

00:52.524 --> 00:55.527
[SPEAKER_02]: Just to know that's being handled in case there was any bad blood from this.

00:58.928 --> 01:00.009
[SPEAKER_02]: So this will blow over.

01:01.310 --> 01:08.095
[SPEAKER_02]: But this was my one for you pulling you out because I didn't want it to get any worse.

01:09.435 --> 01:12.638
[SPEAKER_02]: And here I thought I was ending my life.

01:12.678 --> 01:14.119
[SPEAKER_02]: My life was ending.

01:16.260 --> 01:16.440
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh.

01:18.482 --> 01:18.882
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

01:19.262 --> 01:24.706
[SPEAKER_02]: No, you guys do have maybe a little bit of preconceived notion of

01:25.874 --> 01:30.276
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't know who I am or what I am, but remember when I shouted out and you thought I was the asshole?

01:30.897 --> 01:31.457
[SPEAKER_02]: It is Jude.

01:31.717 --> 01:32.938
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not Jude, okay?

01:34.699 --> 01:39.241
[SPEAKER_02]: I mean, I'll follow the law, and it is, and there's no reason.

01:39.362 --> 01:39.542
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

01:40.682 --> 01:46.786
[SPEAKER_02]: You have no reason to fear me unless you cross somebody besides me that I'm loyal to.

01:48.046 --> 01:49.747
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the only thing we should fear.

01:51.809 --> 01:52.309
[SPEAKER_02]: Fair enough.

01:52.629 --> 01:54.190
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, I appreciate you getting me out there.

01:56.103 --> 02:00.306
[SPEAKER_02]: You want them here for this little next bit?

02:00.446 --> 02:03.067
[SPEAKER_00]: Tyrus walks out and you find the two of them in an alleyway.

02:04.408 --> 02:09.791
[SPEAKER_00]: Gouge actually has his arm around Folsom's shoulder and is talking to him in not a mean way.

02:09.811 --> 02:11.572
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not sure if that's a good sign or not.

02:11.952 --> 02:14.433
[SPEAKER_02]: So I see him come up.

02:14.573 --> 02:17.755
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm just gonna throw up Knuckles to him.

02:18.676 --> 02:20.016
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

02:20.777 --> 02:21.878
[SPEAKER_01]: Is this part where I get stabbed?

02:27.959 --> 02:28.600
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll tell Ty.

02:29.300 --> 02:32.182
[SPEAKER_01]: Great song, but not the best crowd, brother.

02:32.443 --> 02:33.804
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

02:33.844 --> 02:39.108
[SPEAKER_01]: Hey, I read the room and pulled them out, and that was just all for show to get them out.

02:40.409 --> 02:46.774
[SPEAKER_01]: I told him it was a joke and bought him all more beer, so I think that'll cure a lot.

02:49.156 --> 02:49.476
[SPEAKER_01]: All right.

02:50.797 --> 02:51.358
[SPEAKER_01]: Where's Mary?

02:51.398 --> 02:52.258
[SPEAKER_01]: Did you leave him in there?

02:52.398 --> 02:52.759
[SPEAKER_01]: I did.

02:52.799 --> 02:55.401
[SPEAKER_01]: He was talking to Owen, so...

02:56.982 --> 02:57.529
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you mind?

02:57.772 --> 02:58.238
[SPEAKER_02]: You guys...

02:59.050 --> 03:00.691
[SPEAKER_02]: Don't have business in the barracks, or do you?

03:00.931 --> 03:01.931
[SPEAKER_01]: No, let's find it with a bar.

03:02.752 --> 03:04.053
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you go grab Merrick?

03:04.233 --> 03:05.293
[SPEAKER_02]: I got a word with him.

03:05.833 --> 03:11.856
[SPEAKER_02]: We'll be here, come back, and we'll clear these guys with what he just did, and go have a couple.

03:11.876 --> 03:12.997
[SPEAKER_01]: So I'll head back to the bar then?

03:13.697 --> 03:20.061
[SPEAKER_00]: Do I need to head back to- Well, you head back, and actually when you walk in, you see Merrick just shaking Owen's hand and moving towards the door.

03:20.801 --> 03:22.642
[SPEAKER_01]: So I'll just casually step outside the door?

03:23.842 --> 03:25.423
[SPEAKER_01]: So you have to say something in the private room?

03:25.443 --> 03:25.683
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

03:26.044 --> 03:26.144
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh.

03:26.724 --> 03:27.945
[SPEAKER_01]: So we'll step out here.

03:39.018 --> 03:42.959
[SPEAKER_02]: It'll be basically something.

03:43.019 --> 03:44.239
[SPEAKER_02]: Ancient cloak.

03:45.540 --> 03:46.600
[SPEAKER_02]: There's a green stone here.

03:48.700 --> 03:49.681
[SPEAKER_02]: Quite the gem you have here.

03:50.501 --> 03:50.781
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

03:52.301 --> 03:53.821
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't use this as it should be used.

03:55.022 --> 03:55.322
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay?

03:56.682 --> 04:01.623
[SPEAKER_02]: But this thing is probably going to make your songs just a little bit better.

04:02.243 --> 04:02.544
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay?

04:03.484 --> 04:03.964
[SPEAKER_02]: Understood.

04:05.844 --> 04:08.385
[SPEAKER_02]: But this comes with a price if you accept this.

04:09.713 --> 04:10.374
[SPEAKER_02]: The price being?

04:11.214 --> 04:26.126
[SPEAKER_02]: The price being, if we're together and we're in combat and stuff's happening and you're gonna play your tunes or whatever you're gonna do to benefit somebody, I want you to look at me first before you decide.

04:27.707 --> 04:28.368
[SPEAKER_02]: And I'm fair.

04:30.089 --> 04:30.429
[SPEAKER_02]: Okay?

04:31.130 --> 04:31.970
[SPEAKER_02]: And you can trust me.

04:32.871 --> 04:34.312
[SPEAKER_02]: It's up to you whether believe it or not.

04:35.373 --> 04:35.833
[SPEAKER_02]: But listen,

04:36.882 --> 04:41.325
[SPEAKER_02]: When you're gonna throw out something to help somebody or do something, I want you to look at me.

04:41.945 --> 04:45.147
[SPEAKER_02]: If I give a nod, like no, that means I don't need shit.

04:46.348 --> 04:47.088
[SPEAKER_02]: That's all on you.

04:48.109 --> 04:55.913
[SPEAKER_02]: But if you look at me and I'm like, fuck, that means whatever you're doing, you better fucking help me.

04:56.374 --> 04:56.814
[SPEAKER_02]: Understood.

04:58.275 --> 04:59.796
[SPEAKER_02]: You okay with that deal?

05:00.536 --> 05:02.117
[SPEAKER_02]: I'm more than okay with that deal.

05:02.978 --> 05:03.278
[SPEAKER_02]: All right.

05:06.119 --> 05:06.680
[SPEAKER_02]: I owe you one.

05:07.641 --> 05:08.121
[SPEAKER_02]: Or a few.

05:09.062 --> 05:09.503
[SPEAKER_02]: We'll see.

05:09.843 --> 05:12.686
[SPEAKER_02]: Hopefully none, but I'm not that lucky.

05:12.826 --> 05:13.827
[SPEAKER_02]: Or maybe some red-eye.

05:14.027 --> 05:15.709
Ferds is it.

05:15.749 --> 05:15.969
It is.

05:15.989 --> 05:16.370
All right.

